{"title":"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Working_Backwards)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Working Backwards)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Jumping_to_the_Start)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Jumping to the Start)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3(Brute_Force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3(Brute Force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number in each box below is the product of the numbers in the two boxes that touch it in the row above. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/1/9916b1f3d4855379b0ee3bb9d802bfbfba71977e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 = 6\\times5$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" />. What is the missing number in the top row?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/f/6ff959a8ad5edfb7806895cbf5fa087e79899f3f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.8cm); draw((-1,0)--(1,0)--(1,-2)--(-1,-2)--cycle); draw((-2,0)--(0,0)--(0,2)--(-2,2)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(2,0)--(2,2)--(0,2)--cycle); draw((-3,2)--(-1,2)--(-1,4)--(-3,4)--cycle); draw((-1,2)--(1,2)--(1,4)--(-1,4)--cycle); draw((1,2)--(1,4)--(3,4)--(3,2)--cycle); label(&quot;600&quot;,(0,-1)); label(&quot;30&quot;,(-1,1)); label(&quot;6&quot;,(-2,3)); label(&quot;5&quot;,(0,3)); [/asy]\" width=\"228\" height=\"228\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/3/42378a91350e833fafb2a76b7df85d17a25fe36e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Working_Backwards.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Working_Backwards)\">Solution 1 (Working Backwards)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Working Backwards)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the value in the empty box in the middle row be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and the value in the empty box in the top row be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is the answer we're looking for.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/7/c771769746144c26bf1740988d6537ba7a7fc12a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.8cm); draw((-1,0)--(1,0)--(1,-2)--(-1,-2)--cycle); draw((-2,0)--(0,0)--(0,2)--(-2,2)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(2,0)--(2,2)--(0,2)--cycle); draw((-3,2)--(-1,2)--(-1,4)--(-3,4)--cycle); draw((-1,2)--(1,2)--(1,4)--(-1,4)--cycle); draw((1,2)--(1,4)--(3,4)--(3,2)--cycle); label(&quot;600&quot;,(0,-1)); label(&quot;30&quot;,(-1,1)); label(&quot;6&quot;,(-2,3)); label(&quot;5&quot;,(0,3)); label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(1,1)); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(2,3)); [/asy]\" width=\"228\" height=\"228\" />\n</p><p>From the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/7/1773a38ed316e2eaae3d220d9b7839d0d20a8901.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$600 = 30x$\" width=\"79\" height=\"12\" />, making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/1/501e01049152d68121e7508cfdb86e345cc25ed1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 20$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f0aa287aadc370e60cd745aa49e0ec166431b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.8cm); draw((-1,0)--(1,0)--(1,-2)--(-1,-2)--cycle); draw((-2,0)--(0,0)--(0,2)--(-2,2)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(2,0)--(2,2)--(0,2)--cycle); draw((-3,2)--(-1,2)--(-1,4)--(-3,4)--cycle); draw((-1,2)--(1,2)--(1,4)--(-1,4)--cycle); draw((1,2)--(1,4)--(3,4)--(3,2)--cycle); label(&quot;600&quot;,(0,-1)); label(&quot;30&quot;,(-1,1)); label(&quot;6&quot;,(-2,3)); label(&quot;5&quot;,(0,3)); label(&quot;20&quot;,(1,1)); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(2,3)); [/asy]\" width=\"228\" height=\"228\" />\n</p><p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/0/7d097ad027b4be070b5d33145628c5eb2c6dbff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 = 5y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/f/8ef28ed02a20e253bdbc5f8b9d5726c72e6342e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"89\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Jumping_to_the_Start.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Jumping_to_the_Start)\">Solution 2 (Jumping to the Start)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Jumping to the Start)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Another way to do this problem is to realize what makes up the bottommost number. This method doesn't work quite as well for this problem, but in a larger tree, it might be faster. Again, let the value in the empty box in the middle row be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and the value in the empty box in the top row be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is the answer we're looking for.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/7/c771769746144c26bf1740988d6537ba7a7fc12a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.8cm); draw((-1,0)--(1,0)--(1,-2)--(-1,-2)--cycle); draw((-2,0)--(0,0)--(0,2)--(-2,2)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(2,0)--(2,2)--(0,2)--cycle); draw((-3,2)--(-1,2)--(-1,4)--(-3,4)--cycle); draw((-1,2)--(1,2)--(1,4)--(-1,4)--cycle); draw((1,2)--(1,4)--(3,4)--(3,2)--cycle); label(&quot;600&quot;,(0,-1)); label(&quot;30&quot;,(-1,1)); label(&quot;6&quot;,(-2,3)); label(&quot;5&quot;,(0,3)); label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(1,1)); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(2,3)); [/asy]\" width=\"228\" height=\"228\" />\n</p><p>We can write some equations:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/3/d73c65e98e9565d41b24f2734f3272962a63fa2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$600 = 30x\\\\ 30 = 6\\cdot 5\\\\ x = 5y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p>Now we can substitute into the first equation using the two others:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1dbc227d38bd9247e7f1e1b2d7bd649d88e6ac12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$600 = (6\\cdot5)(5y)\\\\ 600= 6\\cdot5\\cdot5\\cdot y\\\\ 600=6\\cdot25\\cdot y\\\\ 600 = 150y\\\\ \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 4} = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"128\" height=\"106\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3.28Brute_Force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3(Brute_Force)\">Solution 3(Brute Force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3(Brute Force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Just try all the answer choices until you get 600\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4tSvBcnv6dA\">https://youtu.be/4tSvBcnv6dA</a> ~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8\" title=\"2013 AMC 8\">2013 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2013\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017232131\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.034 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 162/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2268/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5013/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.751      1 -total\n 56.58%    7.215      1 Template:AMC8_box\n 40.98%    5.226      1 Template:MAA_N